BT /F1 11 Tf 50 740 Td 14 TL
(PulseHR Internal Research Brief) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Topic: Leave request approval friction) Tj T*
(Prepared for: Design + PM, Q2 planning) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Method: 14-question survey sent to all people-managers \(212 respondents, 61% response rate\),) Tj T*
(plus 8 follow-up interviews with a mix of managers and employees.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Key findings) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(68% of managers said they have forgotten about a pending leave request at least once,) Tj T*
(usually because it arrived as one more email in a crowded inbox with no reminder.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Average time from request submitted to request approved was 4.2 days across the sample, with) Tj T*
(wide variance: 71% were resolved within 2 days, but a long tail of 12% took over a week.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Employees consistently described the current status view as unclear - the portal shows) Tj T*
('Pending' with no indication of who it is waiting on or how long that is likely to take.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(A recurring request from managers: let me approve from wherever I already look every day) Tj T*
(\(email or Slack\), not a separate portal I have to remember to open.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Recommendation going into design) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Treat the approval as an inbox-style queue, not a buried settings page, and surface status) Tj T*
(\(who it is with, how long they have had it\) back to the employee without them needing to) Tj T*
(ask.) Tj T*
ET
